{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791028916,"nonce":"qeMC0ZRrQUv3wGMbNfQnisTZRJw=","title":"Rasterize an already-parsed scene, so a caller needn't round-trip markup","message":"An embedder that parses SVG itself has to serialise its shapes back to\nmarkup for blinc_svg, which then parses them again through usvg,\nroxmltree, svgtypes and simplecss. A typed entry point would skip that,\nand if the markup path sat behind its own feature, such a caller could\ndrop usvg and its parsers and keep tiny-skia alone.\n\nProposed by the ashui session, which parses SVG in Haxe — paths, rects\nand circles as path commands, solid and currentColor paints, groups with\nopacity and transform:\n\n    blinc_svg::Scene { view_box: [f32; 4], nodes: Vec\u003cNode\u003e }\n\n    Node::Group { opacity, transform: [f32; 6], children }\n    Node::Path  { commands: Vec\u003cPathCommand\u003e,\n                  fill:   Option\u003c(Paint, FillRule, f32)\u003e,\n                  stroke: Option\u003c(Paint, f32, Cap, Join, f32, f32)\u003e,\n                  transform }\n\n    PathCommand = MoveTo | LineTo | CubicTo | QuadTo\n                | ArcTo { rx, ry, rotation, large, sweep, x, y } | Close\n    Paint       = Solid([f32; 4]) | CurrentColor\n\n    rasterize_scene(\u0026Scene, width, height, current_color) -\u003e RasterizedSvg\n\ntiny-skia directly, fitted and centred the way `RasterizedSvg::from_tree`\nalready does, with group opacity drawn as a layer.\n\nNotes for whoever takes it:\n\n- `CurrentColor` as a paint variant resolved at rasterization is the\n  right shape, and better than what the markup path does: that resolves\n  currentColor by string substitution on the source before usvg sees it.\n- ArcTo needs converting to cubics; tiny-skia has no arc primitive.\n- Gating the markup path behind a `parser` feature is the second half of\n  the ask and the part that actually removes the dependencies. Worth\n  deciding together with `svg_text`, since both are about what an\n  embedder can leave out.\n\nashui asked to be consulted before anyone builds it, in case the API\nshould be shaped differently.","files":null}]}